      {
        "id": "p31-q49-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that $\\tan\\theta=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos 2\\theta}{1+\\cos 2\\theta}}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos 2\\theta}{1+\\cos 2\\theta}}=\\sqrt{\\tan^2\\theta}=\\tan\\theta$.\n\nUse the sine-only expansion in the numerator and the cosine-only expansion in the denominator; $\\tan\\theta>0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos 2\\theta}{1+\\cos 2\\theta}}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-(1-2\\sin^2\\theta)}{1+(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)}}\\\\\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos 2\\theta}{1+\\cos 2\\theta}}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\sin^2\\theta}{2\\cos^2\\theta}}\\\\\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos 2\\theta}{1+\\cos 2\\theta}}&=\\sqrt{\\tan^2\\theta}\\\\\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos 2\\theta}{1+\\cos 2\\theta}}&=\\tan\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $0<\\theta<\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, $\\tan\\theta>0$, so the positive square root is $\\tan\\theta$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q49-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find the exact value of $\\tan 22.5^\\circ$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{3-2\\sqrt2}=\\sqrt2-1$.\n\nApply part (a) with $2\\theta=45^\\circ$ and simplify the positive square root.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan 22.5^\\circ&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos45^\\circ}{1+\\cos45^\\circ}}\\\\\\tan 22.5^\\circ&=\\sqrt{\\frac{2-\\sqrt2}{2+\\sqrt2}}\\\\\\tan 22.5^\\circ&=\\sqrt{\\frac{(2-\\sqrt2)^2}{4-2}}\\\\\\tan 22.5^\\circ&=\\sqrt{3-2\\sqrt2}\\\\\\tan 22.5^\\circ&=\\sqrt2-1.\\end{align*}$$\nHere $3-2\\sqrt2=(\\sqrt2-1)^2$ and $\\sqrt2-1>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      }
    ]
